Troubleshooting Tips
Issue: "No module named 'plugin_base'"

Solution: Ensure you're running from the ~/log-analyzer directory
Check that plugin_base.py exists in the current directory
Issue: "Plugin directory not found"

Solution: Verify the plugins directory exists: ls -la plugins/
Create if missing: mkdir plugins
Issue: Plugins not loading

Solution: Ensure plugin files end with _analyzer.py
Check that each plugin has a get_plugin() function
Verify file permissions: chmod +r plugins/*.py
Issue: No findings in report

Solution: Check log file exists: cat logs/sample.log
Verify log patterns match plugin detection rules
Add debug print statements in plugin analyze() methods
